import Text "mo:core/Text";

mixin () {
  /// Static Markdown documentation of the public backend API.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    let lines : [Text] = [
      "# NAKSwap Sandbox — Backend API",
      "",
      "A **sandbox-only** model of the two-leg swap **any token → ICP (Houdini) →",
      "NAK (NAKSwap router on ICPSwap)**. No real funds move: the ICP ledger, the",
      "NAK ledger, and the ICPSwap pool are all simulated inside the canister.",
      "There is no sign-in, no wallet, and no roles — every endpoint works for any",
      "anonymous visitor.",
      "",
      "## Authentication and authorization",
      "",
      "There is **no authentication**. Every public method is callable by any",
      "caller, including the anonymous principal. No endpoint reads the caller's",
      "identity. The NAK recipient is a principal the user **types** into the",
      "frontend; the backend validates it is a real principal and rejects the",
      "anonymous principal `2vxsx-fae` with the trap",
      "`'Recipient must not be the anonymous principal'`.",
      "",
      "## Public methods",
      "",
      "- `getQuote(tokenSymbol, tokenAmount, routeType)` — query; two-leg quote",
      "  preview. Traps `'Unknown token'` for an unseeded symbol.",
      "- `createOrder(recipient, tokenSymbol, tokenAmount, routeType,",
      "  refundAddress)` — update; returns the new order id. Traps on the anonymous",
      "  recipient and on an unknown token.",
      "- `listOrders(filter)` — query; orders newest-first, optionally filtered by",
      "  router status.",
      "- `getOrder(id)` — query; the full order or `null`.",
      "- `simulateDeposit(id)` — update; the \"I've sent it\" action. Traps",
      "  `'Order not found'`.",
      "- `processOrder(id)` — update; advances the router leg one step and returns",
      "  `#advanced(status)`, `#busy`, or `#noop`. Traps `'Order not found'`.",
      "- `getConfig()` / `setConfig(config)` — read and update the router config.",
      "  `setConfig` traps `'Invalid config: bps out of range'` when",
      "  `slippageBps`/`maxImpactBps` > 10000, and `'Invalid config: order",
      "  bounds'` when `minOrderIcp` = 0 or `maxOrderIcp` < `minOrderIcp`.",
      "- `getTestToggles()` / `setTestToggles(toggles)` — read and update the",
      "  sandbox failure toggles.",
      "- `getSandboxBalances()` — query; pool reserves, router main balances, and",
      "  per-principal balances.",
      "- `listTokens()` — query; the token catalogue.",
      "- `setTokenPrice(symbol, usdMicro)` — update; traps `'Unknown token'`.",
      "- `getIcpPrice()` / `setIcpPrice(usdMicro)` — read and update the ICP price.",
      "- `getNakBalance(principal)` — query; the simulated NAK balance.",
      "- `resetSandbox()` — update; clears orders and reseeds tokens, pool, config,",
      "  and toggles.",
      "",
      "## Units and encodings",
      "",
      "- **Amounts** are in the smallest unit: e8s for ICP, 8-decimal units for NAK,",
      "  and the smallest unit of the source token for `tokenAmount`.",
      "- **USD prices** (`usdMicro`) are micro-dollars: `1_000_000` = $1.00.",
      "- **Timestamps** (`createdAt`, `updatedAt`) are nanoseconds since the epoch",
      "  (`Time.now()`), encoded as `Int`.",
      "- **Account ids** are 64-hex ICP account identifiers.",
      "- **Deposit subaccounts** are 32 bytes: `0x4E 0x41 0x4B` ('NAK'), zeros, then",
      "  the order id big-endian in the last 8 bytes.",
      "- **Basis points** (`slippageBps`, `maxImpactBps`, route fees) are 1/100 of a",
      "  percent.",
      "- Optional fields (`icpIn`, `nakOut`, `block`, `refundReason`,",
      "  `refundAddress`) are `null` until set.",
      "",
      "## Order lifecycle",
      "",
      "Each order has **two legs**.",
      "",
      "**Leg 1 — Houdini** (`houdiniStatus`): `waiting` → `confirming` →",
      "`exchanging` → (`anonymizing` for Private routes) → `completed`. Calling",
      "`simulateDeposit(id)` starts the walk; a dedicated 4-second timer advances",
      "it a step every 4 seconds. On `completed`, the quoted ICP is credited to the",
      "order's deposit account on the simulated ICP ledger. If `simulateDeposit` is",
      "never called, the leg expires after 30 minutes and shows `expired`.",
      "",
      "**Leg 2 — NAKSwap router** (`routerStatus`): `awaitingDeposit` → `swapping`",
      "→ `payoutPending` → `completed`, or `refunded` with a reason. It runs",
      "automatically once the Houdini leg completes (timer, or `processOrder(id)`).",
      "NAK is paid to the typed recipient, or the ICP is refunded to the recipient",
      "with a reason.",
      "",
      "Refund reasons: `tooSmall`, `tooLarge`, `priceImpact{bps}`,",
      "`swapFailed(text)`, `admin`.",
      "",
      "## Polling",
      "",
      "Orders advance asynchronously. Poll `getOrder(id)` or `listOrders(filter)`",
      "and watch `houdiniStatus` / `routerStatus` / `updatedAt`. Terminal router",
      "statuses are `completed` and `refunded`; `needsReview` is a non-terminal",
      "status the router does not currently produce. The Houdini leg is advanced",
      "by a dedicated 4-second timer, while the router leg runs on a 20-second",
      "timer, so a client does not need to call `processOrder` itself.",
      "",
      "## Mutation retry safety",
      "",
      "`processOrder` is idempotent for terminal orders (returns `#noop`). The busy",
      "lock prevents concurrent swaps. `simulateDeposit` is safe to call repeatedly",
      "and only starts the leg once.",
      "",
      "## Errors and limits",
      "",
      "- `createOrder` traps with `'Recipient must not be the anonymous principal'`",
      "  for the anonymous principal, and with `'Unknown token'` for an unseeded",
      "  symbol.",
      "- `setConfig` traps on invalid bounds: `slippageBps`/`maxImpactBps` > 10000,",
      "  `minOrderIcp` = 0, or `maxOrderIcp` < `minOrderIcp`.",
      "- `simulateDeposit` and `processOrder` trap with `'Order not found'` for an",
      "  unknown id.",
      "",
      "## Queryable data (OQL)",
      "",
      "The persisted collections are exposed through the OQL `schema()` /",
      "`execute()` endpoints with per-table authorization (controller-only):",
      "`order`, `token`, `config`, and `sandboxBalance`. These are read by the Data",
      "Intelligence agent, not by end users.",
    ];
    lines.values().join("\n");
  };
};
